// A recipe, written from md-docs/recipes/responsive-navigation.md by scripts/docsite/recipes.py;
// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeResponsiveNavigation(path: "/recipes/responsive-navigation", title: "Make navigation responsive — Recipes", description: "Show navigation links on a wide screen and a menu button on a narrow one, by branching on viewport.") {
    RecipeShell("Make navigation responsive", summary: "A row of links fits a laptop but not a phone. To show the links on a wide screen and a menu button that opens them on a narrow one, branch on `viewport`:", outputs: ["website", "app"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Keep the active tab in the address", to: "/recipes/active-tab-in-the-address"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Keep filters in the address", to: "/recipes/filters-in-the-address"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Build a confirm dialog", to: "/recipes/confirm-dialog")], source: "md-docs/recipes/responsive-navigation.md", how: true, hasVariations: false) {
        code {
            Markdown("**Needs:** nothing besides the page. It claims `/`: paste it into a new project, or replace the starter's `src/pages/Home.wf` with it.")
            CodeBlock(#"page Nav(path: "/", title: "Home", description: "Navigation that fits the screen.") {
    state open = false
    Heading("Home").h1
    if viewport.md {
        Row(gap: .md) {
            Link("Home", to: "/")
            Link("Docs", to: "/docs")
            Link("Pricing", to: "/pricing")
        }
    } else {
        IconButton(icon: "menu", label: "Open navigation", aria-expanded: open, aria-controls: "nav-menu") {
            on click { open = !open }
        }
        show open {
            Stack(gap: .sm, animate: .slideDown, id: "nav-menu") {
                Link("Home", to: "/")
                Link("Docs", to: "/docs")
                Link("Pricing", to: "/pricing")
            }
        }
    }
}

page Docs(path: "/docs", title: "Docs", description: "How it works.") { Heading("Docs").h1 }
page Pricing(path: "/pricing", title: "Pricing", description: "What it costs.") { Heading("Pricing").h1 }"#, title: "wf")
        }
        Markdown("- [`viewport.md`](/learn/07-state-and-reactivity#the-browser-as-values) is true while the window is at least the `md` breakpoint wide. The runtime updates it when a breakpoint is crossed, so the `if` swaps the row for the button as the window narrows.\n- On a narrow screen, the `IconButton` toggles `open`. Its `label:` is the button's accessible name, since the icon has no text, and `aria-expanded: open` tells a screen reader whether the menu it controls (`aria-controls`, the `Stack`'s `id`) is open.\n- `show open` keeps the links in the page and hides them while `open` is false. `animate: .slideDown` plays as they appear.\n\nThe pre-rendered page does not know the window's width, so what depends on `viewport` is drawn once the page is live. For layout alone — a row that becomes a column — prefer [responsive values](/learn/13-styling#responsive-values), which are right in the first paint.\n\n`Docs` and `Pricing` are there so every link lands on a page; in a site of your own the links name the pages you have, and the navigation usually lives in `app`, around the `Router`, so every page shows it.")

    }
}
